  "question": {
    "text": "A heavy ball of mass <math><mi>M</mi></math> is suspended from the ceiling of a car by a light string of mass <math><mi>m</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#8810;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> When the car is at rest, the speed of transverse waves in the string is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> When the car has acceleration <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the wave-speed increases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60.5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo></math> in terms of gravitational acceleration <math><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo></math> is closed to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
